cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the
  metadata from this file.
title: AIGC Detector
subtitle: A local, explainable AI-generated-text detector that runs on CPU
authors:
  - alias: ggg2761367
    name-suffix: "(replace with your real name)"
version: v1.0.1
date-released: "2026-10-29"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ggg2761367/aigc-detector"
url: "https://github.com/ggg2761367/aigc-detector"
abstract: >-
  An open-source AI-generated-text detector combining a
  zero-dependency heuristic engine (surface statistics,
  lexical markers, burstiness) with an optional ONNX int8
  multilingual classifier. Runs fully offline on CPU; no
  text is uploaded anywhere. Includes document parsing
  (docx/pdf), invisible-character watermark detection,
  sentence-level highlights, and calibration support.
keywords:
  - AI-generated text detection
  - machine-generated text
  - ONNX
  - Chinese NLP
  - text forensics
